<p>In the latest turn in the US-Israel war with Iran, Iranian forces intensified attacks on commercial shipping and energy-related targets around the Persian Gulf. Strikes were reported in and around the Strait of Hormuz and Iraqi waters, renewing fears of supply disruptions. Oil prices climbed back above $100 a barrel, even as the United States and other countries moved to release strategic reserves to steady markets. Several ships were reported hit. One attack on a US-owned oil tanker in Iraqi waters killed a crew member—identified by Indian outlets as an Indian national—while other crew were rescued and taken to Basra. Regional authorities took emergency steps affecting ports and terminals, and reports also described airstrikes in cities including Beirut and Tehran as fighting continued on multiple fronts. The UN Security Council called for Iran to halt strikes on Gulf neighbors, while President Donald Trump said Iran was nearing defeat but signaled operations would not end immediately.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kfnOXAVFBByerWqi7-IR8LimGieFCNU2XOp21555jptWu0uabtwN975yhqqGVorIij1BSRxEO-ODmHFvVfpxbjczkP92fxzbE2iBhrjXAWtwjKbq-gIztA9Tz0M7LZ-Gyj4Q-6n4qafu8PhvT0a5TSjyQiE' alt='Damage and emergency response after reported strikes as Gulf tensions rise.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Port disruptions: Iraq paused operations at all its oil ports after attacks on tankers in Iraqi waters, and Oman evacuated ships from its main oil export terminal—an early sign of how fast the conflict is spilling into critical energy logistics.</li><li>Price warning: Iran warned the world to brace for oil prices as high as $200 a barrel, seeking to pressure the US and Israel by amplifying global economic pain.</li><li>Fuel facilities hit: After tankers were struck, a fresh wave of drone and missile attacks hit Gulf fuel facilities and other economic infrastructure, adding to market anxiety about supply and logistics disruption.</li><li>Maritime enforcement: Iranian forces, including the Revolutionary Guards, said they fired on merchant ships that ignored orders. Reports said multiple vessels were hit in Gulf waters.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Nations Security Council: The Security Council demanded that Iran halt strikes on Gulf neighbors as attacks widened to infrastructure and shipping. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/iran-targets-busiest-international-airport-top-body-demands-130958098'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Iranian officials: Iran said it was ready for a prolonged “war of attrition” that could threaten the global economy by squeezing regional energy supplies. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/11/iran-escalates-attacks-on-infrastructure-and-transport-networks-across-the-gulf'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said US forces had “won” and that Iran was “pretty much at the end of the line,” while also signaling there would be no quick end to operations. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/trump-iran-signal-no-quick-end-war-tankers-burn-iraqi-waters-2026-03-12/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>International Energy Agency: The IEA urged a large, coordinated release of strategic oil reserves to soften the shock and keep supplies moving amid disruptions. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1w5141vx53o'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-targets-fuel-facilities-sending-oil-soaring-again'>Iran targets fuel facilities, sending oil soaring again</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/12/world/iran-war-news-trump-oil-israel'>Iran War Live Updates: Oil Tops $100 a Barrel as Attacks Spread Across Middle East</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1w5141vx53o'>Oil price jumps despite deal to release record amount of reserves</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/87a06d69-7cb2-4aaf-82ff-da0bf8be